From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA/HIP: trim idle MMVQ waves without remapping work

Keep the compile-time eight-wave RDNA4 MMVQ geometry, but launch only the
leading waves whose stock k-loop has work. Nemotron's K=2688 Q5_0 matrices need
six waves and its K=1856 Q5_0 matrices need four. Slots for omitted waves are
filled with +0.0f before the unchanged stock reduction, preserving active
threads' k-block assignments and floating-point operation order.

GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_NO_TRIM=1 restores the stock launch for same-binary A/B tests.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu | 92 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 81 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
index 0589e65bd..1eeb02a86 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
